  planner_response {
    response: "### Completed Enhancements & Verification Summary\n\nAll requested updates and refinements for **HAYAT** have been implemented, tested, and verified:\n\n---\n\n### Key Updates Implemented\n\n1. **Conditional Step 2 & Risk Engine Alignment**\n   - In Step 2 (\"Your journey\"), the question *\"How long have you been actively trying to conceive?\"* appears **strictly if the user chose \"Actively trying currently\"**.\n   - If the user selects \"Not right now\" or \"Planning for the future\", the timeline question is hidden and replaced with a supportive message (*\"Planning ahead is a great time to check in and optimize lifestyle factors early\"*).\n   - In `src/engine/riskEngine.ts`, `tryingDuration` is only factored into the score when `familyPlanning === \'trying\'`. The Privacy Dashboard data inventory similarly only lists the timeline if actively trying.\n\n2. **Human-Readable Labels Everywhere (No Raw Enums)**\n   - Added `src/utils/formatters.ts` with `formatLabel()` and `getHumanReadableInventory()`.\n   - All screens (Results, Explainability contributions, Privacy Dashboard Data Inventory, Clinician Printable Summary, and Export Data) display human-readable strings (e.g., *\"18 to 24 years\"*, *\"Actively trying currently\"*, *\"Under 3 months\"* rather than `18-24`, `trying`, `under_3`).\n\n3. **Responsive Top Navigation & Hamburger Below 1280px**\n   - Refactored `Navbar.tsx` with `whitespace-nowrap`, tighter padding, and responsive constraints.\n   - The \"Front Door\" badge is now hidden below 1280px (`xl`) so it never crowds the row.\n   - On screens below 1280px (covering 375px, 768px, and smaller laptops), navigation automatically collapses to a mobile drawer / hamburger menu with zero wrapping or overlaps.\n\n4. **Factor-Consistent Results & Triage Wording**\n   - In `riskEngine.ts`, triage reasoning is generated from the actual factors present: when modifiable factors exist in a low risk band, the explanation states *\"A few modifiable factors were found; small everyday changes may help support your overall reproductive wellness\"* rather than only claiming protective habits.\n\n5. **Missing Fields Added**\n   - **Step 3 (Daily Life):** Added **Stress level (1-5 selector)** and **Recreational substance use (None / Occasional / Regular / Prefer not to say)**. Both wire directly into the risk engine (+7 for high stress, +14 for regular substances) and are reflected in the explainability panel.\n   - **Step 4 (Body & Metabolic):** Added optional **Waist size concern (Yes / No / Prefer not to say)**.\n   - Calculated BMI displays softly under height/weight once both are entered (*\"Your calculated BMI is about 24.5: In the typical range\"* without judgment), and feeds directly into the risk engine.\n\n6. **Consistent Max-Width & Desktop Layout**\n   - Unified wizard card containers to `max-w-3xl mx-auto` for a balanced, centered desktop presentation.\n\n7. **Trust, Copy & Cautious Medical Language**\n   - Replaced all clinic references with clearly fictional demo clinics (*\"Al Noor Men\'s Health Clinic (Demo Clinic)\"*, *\"Marina Andrology & Family Health Centre (Demo Clinic)\"*).\n   - Relabeled the section to **\"Sample clinics (demo data)\"** with an explicit *\"Sample data\"* badge, and labeled wait times as *\"Illustrative wait: ~2 days\"*.\n   - Softened clinical claims to cautious language (*\"may be associated with\"*, *\"can influence\"*).\n   - In the Privacy Dashboard, changed the header to **\"You\'re in control\"** and renamed the column to **\"Why we use it\"** with plain-language explanations.\n\n8. **Evidence Page & Deterministic Real Engine Simulation**\n   - Relabeled the safety recall card to: **\"Red-Flag Safety Rule: 20/20 urgent cases routed to urgent assessment (guaranteed by design, rule-based override)\"**.\n   - The 500 synthetic cases are now generated via a seeded pseudo-random generator and processed directly through the live `assessRisk()` function.\n   - Enlarged the axis labels and widened the label column on the completion funnel chart to eliminate overlap.\n\n9. **Readability & WCAG AA Contrast**\n   - Increased minimum body font size to 14px and caption sizes to 12px across all pages.\n   - Enhanced contrast colors in `src/index.css` (`--text-main: #F1F7F7`, `--text-muted: #A8BCC2` in dark mode; high-contrast `#0B1921` / `#334852` in light mode; improved input placeholder contrast).\n   - Increased footer disclaimer text size to 12px/14px.\n\n---\n\n### Verification Results\n\n- **`tsc --noEmit`:** 0 errors.\n- **`compile_applet`:** Build succeeded.\n- **`restart_dev_server`:** Fresh dev server running on port 3000.\n- **Responsive verification:** 375px (mobile), 768px (tablet), 1280px (laptop), 1440px (desktop) verified."
    modified_response: "### Completed Enhancements & Verification Summary\n\nAll requested updates and refinements for **HAYAT** have been implemented, tested, and verified:\n\n---\n\n### Key Updates Implemented\n\n1. **Conditional Step 2 & Risk Engine Alignment**\n   - In Step 2 (\"Your journey\"), the question *\"How long have you been actively trying to conceive?\"* appears **strictly if the user chose \"Actively trying currently\"**.\n   - If the user selects \"Not right now\" or \"Planning for the future\", the timeline question is hidden and replaced with a supportive message (*\"Planning ahead is a great time to check in and optimize lifestyle factors early\"*).\n   - In `src/engine/riskEngine.ts`, `tryingDuration` is only factored into the score when `familyPlanning === \'trying\'`. The Privacy Dashboard data inventory similarly only lists the timeline if actively trying.\n\n2. **Human-Readable Labels Everywhere (No Raw Enums)**\n   - Added `src/utils/formatters.ts` with `formatLabel()` and `getHumanReadableInventory()`.\n   - All screens (Results, Explainability contributions, Privacy Dashboard Data Inventory, Clinician Printable Summary, and Export Data) display human-readable strings (e.g., *\"18 to 24 years\"*, *\"Actively trying currently\"*, *\"Under 3 months\"* rather than `18-24`, `trying`, `under_3`).\n\n3. **Responsive Top Navigation & Hamburger Below 1280px**\n   - Refactored `Navbar.tsx` with `whitespace-nowrap`, tighter padding, and responsive constraints.\n   - The \"Front Door\" badge is now hidden below 1280px (`xl`) so it never crowds the row.\n   - On screens below 1280px (covering 375px, 768px, and smaller laptops), navigation automatically collapses to a mobile drawer / hamburger menu with zero wrapping or overlaps.\n\n4. **Factor-Consistent Results & Triage Wording**\n   - In `riskEngine.ts`, triage reasoning is generated from the actual factors present: when modifiable factors exist in a low risk band, the explanation states *\"A few modifiable factors were found; small everyday changes may help support your overall reproductive wellness\"* rather than only claiming protective habits.\n\n5. **Missing Fields Added**\n   - **Step 3 (Daily Life):** Added **Stress level (1-5 selector)** and **Recreational substance use (None / Occasional / Regular / Prefer not to say)**. Both wire directly into the risk engine (+7 for high stress, +14 for regular substances) and are reflected in the explainability panel.\n   - **Step 4 (Body & Metabolic):** Added optional **Waist size concern (Yes / No / Prefer not to say)**.\n   - Calculated BMI displays softly under height/weight once both are entered (*\"Your calculated BMI is about 24.5: In the typical range\"* without judgment), and feeds directly into the risk engine.\n\n6. **Consistent Max-Width & Desktop Layout**\n   - Unified wizard card containers to `max-w-3xl mx-auto` for a balanced, centered desktop presentation.\n\n7. **Trust, Copy & Cautious Medical Language**\n   - Replaced all clinic references with clearly fictional demo clinics (*\"Al Noor Men\'s Health Clinic (Demo Clinic)\"*, *\"Marina Andrology & Family Health Centre (Demo Clinic)\"*).\n   - Relabeled the section to **\"Sample clinics (demo data)\"** with an explicit *\"Sample data\"* badge, and labeled wait times as *\"Illustrative wait: ~2 days\"*.\n   - Softened clinical claims to cautious language (*\"may be associated with\"*, *\"can influence\"*).\n   - In the Privacy Dashboard, changed the header to **\"You\'re in control\"** and renamed the column to **\"Why we use it\"** with plain-language explanations.\n\n8. **Evidence Page & Deterministic Real Engine Simulation**\n   - Relabeled the safety recall card to: **\"Red-Flag Safety Rule: 20/20 urgent cases routed to urgent assessment (guaranteed by design, rule-based override)\"**.\n   - The 500 synthetic cases are now generated via a seeded pseudo-random generator and processed directly through the live `assessRisk()` function.\n   - Enlarged the axis labels and widened the label column on the completion funnel chart to eliminate overlap.\n\n9. **Readability & WCAG AA Contrast**\n   - Increased minimum body font size to 14px and caption sizes to 12px across all pages.\n   - Enhanced contrast colors in `src/index.css` (`--text-main: #F1F7F7`, `--text-muted: #A8BCC2` in dark mode; high-contrast `#0B1921` / `#334852` in light mode; improved input placeholder contrast).\n   - Increased footer disclaimer text size to 12px/14px.\n\n---\n\n### Verification Results\n\n- **`tsc --noEmit`:** 0 errors.\n- **`compile_applet`:** Build succeeded.\n- **`restart_dev_server`:** Fresh dev server running on port 3000.\n- **Responsive verification:** 375px (mobile), 768px (tablet), 1280px (laptop), 1440px (desktop) verified."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
