  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Assessing React Compatibility**\n\nI\'m now investigating React 19 compatibility, specifically with `@react-three/fiber`. I\'ve found that version 9 should work, so I\'m also considering combining several installations into a single `install_applet_package` call, incorporating `three` and `@types/three` alongside `@react-three/fiber`.\n\n\n**Evaluating Package Combinations**\n\nI\'m now determining the most effective approach to handle the dependencies. My current focus is streamlining the installation process. I will test a consolidated `install_applet_package` call encompassing `three`, `@types/three`, and `@react-three/fiber` to ensure seamless compatibility with React 19 and confirm that `@react-three/fiber` v9 integrates properly. I\'ll remember to leave `IsDevDependency` as false. Also, I\'m considering if I should use `gsap` or just rely on the installed `motion`. The goal is to efficiently fulfill the animated dotted wave hero component requirements, with a plan to support fallbacks for performance.\n\n\n"
