  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refactoring Color Strategy**\n\nI\'m realizing the current color implementation is creating an unintentional dark-mode default, due to hardcoded color values. My focus is now on establishing a more robust system for light and dark theme contrast. I want to decouple these theme choices from the individual components.\n\n\n**Defining Color Values**\n\nI\'ve established the foundation in `src/index.css` using semantic CSS variables. I\'m prioritizing WCAG AA contrast for both the default \"sand\" light and the \"charcoal\" dark themes, making sure they work consistently throughout the design. I have specifically set the base values for light mode and am analyzing contrast ratios for various text/background combinations.\n\n\n**Defining Dark and Light Themes**\n\nI\'ve finalized the dark theme color definitions, ensuring each element aligns with WCAG AA standards. The muted text on the card background has a 7.5:1 contrast ratio, while the accent color passes the same requirements in the deep background. The borders are now adjusted with rgba to be more subtle. I\'ve chosen risk band colors, too, using icons, in sage green, amber, terracotta, and crimson in light, with matching dark values. I\'m focusing on consistency.\n\n\n**Implementing Font Choices**\n\nI\'ve specified the fonts in `index.html`, including `Outfit`, `Fraunces`, `Inter`, `Noto Sans Devanagari`, and `IBM Plex Sans Arabic`. I have the body font at 16px minimum and am working on implementing language-specific font stacks. I am also working on paper-like matte cards with a `.paper-card` class, including a soft background and hairline borders.\n\n\n**Designing Hero Component**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the hero section\'s visual elements using Three.js and React Three Fiber. I\'m building a Points mesh with layered sine waves, rendering roughly 6,000 points in taupe, adjusting the colors for light and dark modes, and ensuring smooth parallax. Rendering will pause when the tab isn\'t visible, and throttles when active. I\'m integrating the headline, incorporating a serif accent for emphasis while ensuring accurate i18n support.\n\n\n**Refining Survey Flow**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the user interface for the survey. I\'m prioritizing a single question per screen with large, tappable cards and a \"Why we ask\" expander. I am ensuring that the existing question structure and conditional logic are maintained. Keyboard navigation is a key consideration with number keys selecting options, Enter advancing, and Escape triggering a Quick Hide. The progress indicator will also be shaped.\n\n\n**Designing Results Component**\n\nI\'m now implementing the results section, starting with a scroll-based story using `motion/react` for reveals. I plan to use `initial`, `whileInView`, and `viewport` for a smooth effect respecting reduced motion preferences. It will start with a red-flag card with a ShieldAlert icon, then a screening disclaimer, and then a risk band gauge animation. The factor bars will animate one by one, with direction icons, and links to change factors.\n\n\n**Designing What-If Panel**\n\nI am now focusing on building the interactive \"WHAT-IF\" panel. I\'m implementing sliders and toggles for various modifiable factors like exercise, sleep, smoking, alcohol, heat exposure, and stress. Modifying these factors triggers an on-device risk assessment, displaying the \"Before \342\206\222 After\" risk band and score in an animated transition. A clear disclaimer clarifies that this is an illustration and not medical advice.\n\n\n**Implementing Additional Layouts**\n\nI\'m now integrating a screen flow: \"Screened \342\206\222 Booked \342\206\222 Assessed \342\206\222 Follow-up\" with a discreet teleconsultation widget, and sample clinics labeled \"Sample clinics (demo data)\". I\'m working to ensure a privacy dashboard layout with \"What left your device\" section with explicit status messages, and export/delete buttons. I\'m also ensuring evidence is represented with accessible charts.\n\nI will also be implementing the quick hide feature. I have also added a button for quick hide.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
