  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\nRedesign the **visual and interaction layer** of the existing **HAYAT** male reproductive health front-door React/TypeScript/Vite/Tailwind app in one pass without modifying the risk engine rules (`src/engine/riskEngine.ts`), service layer (`src/services/api.ts`), i18n keys (`src/i18n/*`), or safety/consent logic.\n\nCore deliverables requested:\n1. **Visual Identity**:\n   - **Warm \"sand\" LIGHT theme as DEFAULT**: background `#E8E1D5`, surface `#F4EFE6`, card `#FBF8F2`, primary text `#2B2420`, muted text `#6B5F57` (WCAG AA compliant), primary brand taupe `#7A645C`, accent teal `#1F8A7D` (plus `#156A60` for small teal text on light sand to guarantee AA contrast).\n   - **Polished warm charcoal DARK theme toggle**: deep warm charcoal (`#171412`, `#1F1B18`, `#27221E`), not neon.\n   - Calm, accessible risk band colors (Low green, Moderate amber, Elevated orange, Urgent red) always paired with an icon + text.\n   - Typography: `Outfit` headings, `Fraunces` serif accent for hero emphasis words, `Inter` body at `16px` minimum, `Noto Sans Devanagari` for Hindi, `IBM Plex Sans Arabic` for Arabic (RTL).\n   - Replace neon glass cards with soft, matte, paper-like cards (`.paper-card`: subtle shadow, 20\342\200\22324px radius, generous whitespace, hairline borders, no heavy glow).\n2. **Hero with WebGL (Landing Page)**:\n   - Full-width hero with animated dotted wave using `@react-three/fiber` + `three`: a `Points` mesh of ~6,000 points displaced by layered sine waves, taupe on sand (or warm taupe on charcoal), slowly flowing with subtle mouse/touch parallax.\n   - Lazy-loaded via `React.lazy` + `Suspense`, DPR capped at `1.5`, pauses rendering when tab is hidden (`visibilitychange`), throttled `frameloop=\"demand\"`.\n   - Static CSS/SVG dotted-wave fallback when `prefers-reduced-motion`, no WebGL support, or low-power devices (`navigator.hardwareConcurrency <= 2`).\n   - Keep headline `\"A private first step for men\'s reproductive health.\"` (supporting i18n + Fraunces serif accent), sublines, two CTA buttons, trust pills, and 3 demo-persona buttons.\n3. **Wizard Redesign (`src/pages/WizardPage.tsx`)**:\n   - **ONE question per screen**, large heading, big tappable option cards (`min-h-[56px]`), `\"Why we ask\"` expander, visible `\"Prefer not to say / Skip\"` on every question.\n   - **Auto-advance** after a single-select answer (250ms delay, Back always available). Keep manual Next/Continue for sliders, number inputs, multi-selects, and the conditional non-trying message.\n   - **Keyboard navigation**: number keys (`1`\342\200\223`9`) select options, `Enter` advances/continues, `Esc` triggers Quick Hide.\n   - **Thin wave-line progress indicator** that fills smoothly with `\"Question X of N\"` + small chapter label from the 6 existing sections.\n   - Keep all existing questions, conditional logic (`tryingDuration` only when `familyPlanning === \'trying\'`), and autosave. Smooth slide/fade transitions via `motion/react` respecting `prefers-reduced-motion`.\n4. **Results as a Scroll Story + What-If Panel (`src/pages/ResultsPage.tsx`)**:\n   - Sequential scroll reveals (`motion/react` `whileInView` / staggered reveal respecting `prefers-reduced-motion`): (1) Red-flag card first if applicable, (2) \"screening, not diagnosis\" banner, (3) Risk band gauge animating `0` to target score, (4) \"Why this result?\" factor bars animating in one by one with direction icons & \"You can change this\" tags, (5) 5-level vertical triage ladder with `\"You are here\"` marker and reason, (6) Action plan & \"Questions to ask a doctor\" cards, (7) Action buttons.\n   - **Interactive What-If Panel**: sliders/toggles for modifiable factors (`exerciseDays`, `sleepHours`, `smoking`, `alcohol`, `heatExposure` hot baths/laptop, `stressLevel`). Changing them calls `assessRisk()` live on-device and displays Before \342\206\222 After band and score with animated transition, clearly labeled `\"Illustration only, not medical advice.\"`\n   - Keep Simple/Detailed explanation toggle and \"What we did NOT use\" line.\n5. **Other Screens**:\n   - **Care Navigator**: Matte card layout, clean stepper timeline (`Screened \342\206\222 Booked \342\206\222 Assessed \342\206\222 Follow-up`), sample clinics clearly labeled as sample data.\n   - **Privacy Dashboard**: Friendlier table with plain-language columns, visible **\"What left your device\"** section, clear Export / Delete buttons.\n   - **Evidence**: Cleaner Recharts visualizations using theme CSS variables, direct labels, no squeezed axes, honest **\"Method and limits\"** panel stating simulated results illustrate rule behavior and do not prove real-world accuracy.\n   - **Quick Hide**: Neutral wellness screen, prominent Quick Hide button on mobile (show label on mobile too), plus **double-tap / double-click on the HAYAT logo** shortcut in addition to `Esc`.\n6. **Performance & Accessibility**:\n   - Route-level code splitting (`React.lazy` + `Suspense`), lazy-loaded 3D chunk, no layout shift, WCAG AA contrast in both themes, visible focus rings, 44px+ tap targets, `prefers-reduced-motion` respected everywhere.\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Completed:\n- Installed `three` (`^0.187.0`), `@types/three` (`^0.187.0`), and `@react-three/fiber` (`^9.8.2`) in `/package.json`. Note: `@react-three/drei` was intentionally omitted because raw `three` + `@react-three/fiber` supports `<points>` directly without React 19 peer dependency conflicts.\n- Updated `/index.html`: Added Google Fonts (`Fraunces`, `IBM Plex Sans Arabic`, `Inter`, `Noto Sans Devanagari`, `Outfit`) and removed hardcoded dark `body` classes.\n- Updated `/src/index.css`: Implemented full CSS variable token system for Warm Sand Light default (`:root`) and Warm Charcoal Dark (`.theme-dark`), accessible risk-band variables, language-specific font stacks (`html[lang=\"ar\"]`, `html[lang=\"hi\"]`), `16px` base body font size, `.paper-card` / `.surface-panel` matte card utilities, `:focus-visible` ring, `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)`, and print styles.\n- Updated `/src/store/AppContext.tsx`: Switched initial `theme` state from `\'dark\'` to `\'light\'` and updated `useEffect` to toggle `.theme-dark` class on `document.documentElement`.\n\n### Inspected (Ready to Rewrite/Update):\n- Read `/package.json`, `/src/App.tsx`, `/src/pages/LandingPage.tsx`, `/src/pages/ConsentPage.tsx`, `/src/pages/HowItWorksPage.tsx`, `/src/pages/AnalysingPage.tsx`, `/src/components/RiskGauge.tsx`, `/src/components/FactorBar.tsx`, `/src/components/TriageLadder.tsx`, `/src/components/QuickHideButton.tsx`, `/src/components/QuickHideScreen.tsx`, `/src/components/LangSwitcher.tsx`. (Also from prior turn context: `Navbar.tsx`, `SafetyFooter.tsx`, `WizardPage.tsx`, `ResultsPage.tsx`, `CareNavigatorPage.tsx`, `PrivacyDashboardPage.tsx`, `EvidencePage.tsx`, `ClinicianSummaryModal.tsx`\342\200\224currently all still use hardcoded dark colors like `text-[#EAF4F4]`, `text-[#9FB4BA]`, `bg-[#07131A]`, `glass-panel`, which must be migrated to semantic CSS variables `text-[var(--text-main)]`, `text-[var(--text-muted)]`, `.paper-card`, etc.)\n\n### Remaining to Create / Modify:\n- Create `/src/components/HeroDottedWave.tsx` and `/src/components/HeroWaveWrapper.tsx`.\n- Update `/src/components/QuickHideButton.tsx`, `/src/components/Navbar.tsx`, `/src/components/LangSwitcher.tsx`, `/src/components/SafetyFooter.tsx`, `/src/components/QuickHideScreen.tsx`.\n- Update `/src/components/RiskGauge.tsx`, `/src/components/FactorBar.tsx`, `/src/components/TriageLadder.tsx`, `/src/components/ClinicianSummaryModal.tsx`.\n- Create `/src/components/WhatIfPanel.tsx` (or include cleanly inside `/src/pages/ResultsPage.tsx` as modular component).\n- Rewrite `/src/pages/LandingPage.tsx`, `/src/pages/ConsentPage.tsx`, `/src/pages/WizardPage.tsx`, `/src/pages/AnalysingPage.tsx`, `/src/pages/ResultsPage.tsx`, `/src/pages/CareNavigatorPage.tsx`, `/src/pages/PrivacyDashboardPage.tsx`, `/src/pages/EvidencePage.tsx`, `/src/pages/HowItWorksPage.tsx`.\n- Update `/src/App.tsx` with route-level `React.lazy` + `Suspense` code splitting.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- Prior codebase hardcoded Tailwind arbitrary dark colors (`text-[#EAF4F4]`, `text-[#9FB4BA]`, `bg-white/[0.02]`, `border-white/10`) everywhere instead of CSS variables, causing the light theme to have broken white-on-cream contrast. Every updated component must use CSS variables (`var(--text-main)`, `var(--text-muted)`, `var(--card)`, `var(--surface)`, `var(--brand)`, `var(--accent)`, `var(--accent-text)`, `var(--border-hairline)`) so **both Warm Sand Light (default) and Warm Charcoal Dark** pass WCAG AA seamlessly.\n- With `@react-three/fiber` v9 + `three` + React 19, TypeScript JSX intrinsics (`<points>`, `<bufferGeometry>`, `<pointsMaterial>`) work natively in R3F v9, or we should verify with `tsc --noEmit` (`lint_applet`) after writing `HeroDottedWave.tsx`.\n- `motion` v12 (`motion/react`) provides `AnimatePresence`, `motion`, `useReducedMotion` \342\200\224 use `useReducedMotion()` in Wizard, Analysing, Results scroll reveals, and RiskGauge.\n- `vite.config.ts` uses Vite 8 (`^8.3.0`). Standard `React.lazy(() => import(...))` works with Vite code splitting (handle named exports via `.then(m => ({ default: m.ComponentName }))` or default exports).\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- No errors encountered yet in this turn. Package install of `three`, `@types/three`, `@react-three/fiber` succeeded cleanly.\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- `src/engine/riskEngine.ts`, `src/services/api.ts`, `src/i18n/*.ts`, `src/types/index.ts`, `src/utils/formatters.ts`, `src/data/personas.ts`, and `src/data/syntheticCohort.ts` must NOT have their rules/keys/logic broken. Note: `LandingPage` hero should render `t.heroTitle` with Fraunces serif accent (e.g., if `language === \'en\'` highlight *\"private first step\"* in `<span className=\"font-serif-accent italic font-medium text-[var(--brand)]\">`, while still displaying full `t.heroTitle` cleanly for `hi` and `ar`).\n- In `Navbar.tsx`, implement double-tap / double-click on the HAYAT logo (using `onDoubleClick` + touch double-tap tracking within 350ms so mobile touch works reliably without blocking single-tap home navigation on deliberate single click, or `onDoubleClick` + `onTouchEnd` double-tap detector) to trigger `triggerQuickHide()`. Also make `QuickHideButton` show its text label on mobile (`375px`) clearly while avoiding navbar wrapping (`whitespace-nowrap`, compact spacing).\n\n## 6. Next Steps\nExecute in batched tool calls, then compile, lint, and test via browser/playwright/headless or dev server inspection:\n1. **Create WebGL Hero Components**:\n   - `/src/components/HeroDottedWave.tsx`: R3F `<Canvas dpr={[1, 1.5]} frameloop=\"demand\" camera={{ position: [0, 3.2, 8.5], fov: 48 }}>` with 6,000-point `THREE.BufferGeometry` wave grid, layered sine wave displacement (`useFrame`), mouse/touch parallax, color reactive to `theme` (`#7A645C` on light sand, `#B89F94` on dark charcoal), throttled `invalidate()` at ~28fps paused when `document.hidden`.\n   - `/src/components/HeroWaveWrapper.tsx`: Detects `prefers-reduced-motion`, WebGL capability (`canvas.getContext(\'webgl2\') || canvas.getContext(\'webgl\')`), and `navigator.hardwareConcurrency <= 2`; lazy-loads `HeroDottedWave` with `React.lazy` + `Suspense` falling back to an elegant static SVG dotted wave (`StaticWaveFallback`) with matching taupe points.\n2. **Update Global & Shared Components** (matte `.paper-card`, semantic CSS vars, AA contrast, 44px+ tap targets):\n   - `/src/components/QuickHideButton.tsx` (visible label even at 375px mobile, `min-h-[44px]` or compact accessible target), `/src/components/LangSwitcher.tsx` (RTL-safe dropdown alignment using `end-0`), `/src/components/Navbar.tsx` (double-tap logo Quick Hide + hamburger `<1280px` + matte theme vars), `/src/components/SafetyFooter.tsx` (`14px` text, WCAG AA contrast), `/src/components/QuickHideScreen.tsx` (keep clean light wellness UI).\n   - `/src/components/RiskGauge.tsx` (animates `0` to `score` with count-up number + accessible band color + icon + text), `/src/components/FactorBar.tsx` (matte card, direction icon, \"You can change this\" / \"Not changeable\" tags, Simple/Detailed), `/src/components/TriageLadder.tsx` (vertical connected path with `\"You are here\"` marker and clinical boundaries), `/src/components/ClinicianSummaryModal.tsx` (theme-aware modal chrome + clean print body).\n3. **Update All Pages & Add Code Splitting**:\n   - `/src/pages/LandingPage.tsx`: Full-width hero over `HeroWaveWrapper`, `Fraunces` serif emphasis, trust pills, CTAs, demo personas, Why Earlier Matters, Built Around Trust.\n   - `/src/pages/ConsentPage.tsx`: Matte comparison cards, big tactile consent toggles, 16px readable copy.\n   - `/src/pages/WizardPage.tsx`: Single-question-per-screen architecture (~16\342\200\22318 granular single-question steps dynamically filtered for conditional `tryingDuration` when `familyPlanning === \'trying\'`, plus a supportive transitional card when `not_now`/`planning`), thin SVG wave-line progress bar (`Question X of N` + chapter label), `min-h-[56px]` option cards, `\"Why we ask\"` expander, visible `\"Prefer not to say / Skip\"` on every question, 250ms auto-advance on single-select, keyboard shortcuts (`1`-`9`, `Enter`, `Esc`), `AnimatePresence` slide/fade transitions respecting `prefers-reduced-motion`.\n   - `/src/pages/AnalysingPage.tsx`: Matte card, reduced-motion-safe animation.\n   - `/src/components/WhatIfPanel.tsx` + `/src/pages/ResultsPage.tsx`: Scroll-story sequential reveals (`whileInView`), prominent red-flag card first, banner, animated gauge, staggered factor bars, What-If interactive panel (live `assessRisk` before \342\206\222 after comparison, `\"Illustration only, not medical advice.\"` label), vertical triage ladder, action plan, clinician summary/delete/care navigator buttons.\n   - `/src/pages/CareNavigatorPage.tsx`: Matte stepper timeline (`Screened \342\206\222 Booked \342\206\222 Assessed \342\206\222 Follow-up`), discreet teleconsultation card, Sample clinics with Sample data badge.\n   - `/src/pages/PrivacyDashboardPage.tsx`: Friendlier plain-language table, visible **\"What left your device\"** card/section, live consent toggles, Export JSON & Delete Data.\n   - `/src/pages/EvidencePage.tsx`: Theme-aware Recharts colors (`var(--chart-axis)`, `var(--chart-grid)`), readable funnel labels, **\"Method and limits\"** panel clearly explaining simulated rule behavior vs real-world clinical accuracy.\n   - `/src/pages/HowItWorksPage.tsx`: Matte paper cards, 16px body, FAQ accordion.\n   - `/src/App.tsx`: Lazy-load route pages via `React.lazy` + `Suspense`.\n4. **Build, Lint, and Thoroughly Verify Everything**:\n   - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`).\n   - Run `restart_dev_server` and verify live app in a headless browser (or check Playwright/Chromium availability via `run_command` to inspect console errors and test all user flows & viewports `375`, `768`, `1280`, `1440`, RTL Arabic, Hindi, Dark/Light toggle, Wizard single-question auto-advance + keyboard nav + conditional branch, What-If panel, Quick Hide button/Esc/double-tap, Privacy export/delete, Evidence charts, Clinician summary). Fix any console errors, TypeScript errors, or layout overflows before final reply.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Do NOT ask the user any questions; complete everything in one continuous pass.\n- Do NOT alter risk engine scoring rules (`src/engine/riskEngine.ts`), service contracts (`src/services/api.ts`), i18n dictionary keys (`src/i18n/*`), or safety/consent rules.\n- Ensure `prefers-reduced-motion`, WCAG AA contrast on both themes, RTL Arabic (`dir=\"rtl\"`), `16px` body font minimum, 44px+ tap targets, and zero console/TypeScript errors.\n- Co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` on the final verification check, and do not report completion until every item in section 7 (\"VERIFY YOURSELF AND FIX FAILURES\") is verified.\n</summary>"
