  planner_response {
    response: "The visual and interaction layer of **HAYAT** has been redesigned while keeping the existing risk engine rules, service layer, i18n keys, and safety/consent logic intact.\n\n### Summary of Updates\n\n1. **Warm Sand Light Default & Warm Charcoal Dark Toggle**\n   - Switched the default theme to a warm sand light palette (`#E8E1D5` background, `#F4EFE6` surface, `#FBF8F2` paper cards, `#2B2420` primary text, `#6B5F57` muted text, `#7A645C` taupe brand, `#1F8A7D` / `#156A60` teal accent) with a toggleable warm charcoal dark theme.\n   - Replaced neon/glass styling across components and pages with matte paper cards (`.paper-card`, `.surface-panel`), subtle shadows, 20\342\200\22322px radii, hairline borders, and 16px+ readable body typography (`Outfit`, `Fraunces` serif accent, `Inter`, `Noto Sans Devanagari` for Hindi, and `IBM Plex Sans Arabic` for RTL Arabic).\n   - Paired all risk band indicators with icons and text labels in addition to accessible colors.\n\n2. **WebGL Dotted-Wave Hero**\n   - Built `HeroDottedWave` using `@react-three/fiber` and `three` with a 6,000-point `Points` mesh animated by layered sine waves and pointer parallax, lazy-loaded via `React.lazy` + `Suspense`, DPR capped at `1.5`, throttled demand rendering, and paused when the tab is hidden (`document.hidden`).\n   - Added `HeroWaveWrapper` with a static SVG dotted-wave fallback when `prefers-reduced-motion`, missing WebGL support, or low-power hardware is detected.\n   - Kept the hero headline, subline, CTA buttons, trust pills, and demo-persona launcher row.\n\n3. **One-Question-Per-Screen Wizard**\n   - Redesigned `WizardPage` to present one question per screen with `min-h-[56px]` numbered option cards, a thin SVG wave-line progress indicator (`Question X of N` + chapter label), a `\"Why we ask this\"` expander, and `\"Prefer not to say / Skip\"` on every screen.\n   - Added 250ms auto-advance on single-select choices, keyboard navigation (`1`\342\200\223`9` to select options, `Enter` to continue, `Esc` for Quick Hide), `AnimatePresence` transitions respecting `prefers-reduced-motion`, and preserved conditional `tryingDuration` branching and autosave.\n\n4. **Results Scroll Story & Interactive What-If Panel**\n   - Structured `ResultsPage` as a scroll story with sequential `whileInView` reveals: urgent red-flag card first when triggered, `\"screening, not a medical diagnosis\"` banner, animated `0 \342\206\222 score` `RiskGauge`, staggered `FactorBar` items with Simple/Detailed views, vertical 5-level `TriageLadder` with a `\"You are here\"` marker, action plan, and doctor questions.\n   - Added `WhatIfPanel` with live sliders and toggles for modifiable factors (`exerciseDays`, `sleepHours`, `smoking`, `alcohol`, `heatExposure`, `stressLevel`), calling `assessRisk()` on-device to show Before \342\206\222 After band and score changes with an `\"Illustration only, not medical advice.\"` notice.\n\n5. **Care Navigator, Privacy, Evidence & Quick Hide**\n   - Updated `CareNavigatorPage` with matte cards, an interactive 4-step pathway timeline, discreet teleconsultation booking, and `\"Sample data\"` badges on fictional clinics.\n   - Updated `PrivacyDashboardPage` with a plain-language inventory table, a visible **\"What left your device\"** panel, live consent toggles, JSON export, and full local wipe.\n   - Updated `EvidencePage` charts to use theme CSS variables and direct bar labels, paired with a **\"Method and limits\"** disclosure noting simulated rules do not prove real-world clinical accuracy.\n   - Updated `Navbar` and `QuickHideButton` so the Quick Hide label remains visible on mobile screens and double-tapping/double-clicking the HAYAT logo also activates Quick Hide alongside `Esc`.\n\n6. **Code Splitting & Verification**\n   - Added route-level `React.lazy` + `Suspense` splitting in `App.tsx` (separating `HeroDottedWave`, `EvidencePage`, and page routes into distinct chunks).\n   - Verified `compile_applet` (`vite build`), `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`), engine/conditional/i18n checks via `tsx`, and restarted the dev server cleanly on port 3000."
    modified_response: "The visual and interaction layer of **HAYAT** has been redesigned while keeping the existing risk engine rules, service layer, i18n keys, and safety/consent logic intact.\n\n### Summary of Updates\n\n1. **Warm Sand Light Default & Warm Charcoal Dark Toggle**\n   - Switched the default theme to a warm sand light palette (`#E8E1D5` background, `#F4EFE6` surface, `#FBF8F2` paper cards, `#2B2420` primary text, `#6B5F57` muted text, `#7A645C` taupe brand, `#1F8A7D` / `#156A60` teal accent) with a toggleable warm charcoal dark theme.\n   - Replaced neon/glass styling across components and pages with matte paper cards (`.paper-card`, `.surface-panel`), subtle shadows, 20\342\200\22322px radii, hairline borders, and 16px+ readable body typography (`Outfit`, `Fraunces` serif accent, `Inter`, `Noto Sans Devanagari` for Hindi, and `IBM Plex Sans Arabic` for RTL Arabic).\n   - Paired all risk band indicators with icons and text labels in addition to accessible colors.\n\n2. **WebGL Dotted-Wave Hero**\n   - Built `HeroDottedWave` using `@react-three/fiber` and `three` with a 6,000-point `Points` mesh animated by layered sine waves and pointer parallax, lazy-loaded via `React.lazy` + `Suspense`, DPR capped at `1.5`, throttled demand rendering, and paused when the tab is hidden (`document.hidden`).\n   - Added `HeroWaveWrapper` with a static SVG dotted-wave fallback when `prefers-reduced-motion`, missing WebGL support, or low-power hardware is detected.\n   - Kept the hero headline, subline, CTA buttons, trust pills, and demo-persona launcher row.\n\n3. **One-Question-Per-Screen Wizard**\n   - Redesigned `WizardPage` to present one question per screen with `min-h-[56px]` numbered option cards, a thin SVG wave-line progress indicator (`Question X of N` + chapter label), a `\"Why we ask this\"` expander, and `\"Prefer not to say / Skip\"` on every screen.\n   - Added 250ms auto-advance on single-select choices, keyboard navigation (`1`\342\200\223`9` to select options, `Enter` to continue, `Esc` for Quick Hide), `AnimatePresence` transitions respecting `prefers-reduced-motion`, and preserved conditional `tryingDuration` branching and autosave.\n\n4. **Results Scroll Story & Interactive What-If Panel**\n   - Structured `ResultsPage` as a scroll story with sequential `whileInView` reveals: urgent red-flag card first when triggered, `\"screening, not a medical diagnosis\"` banner, animated `0 \342\206\222 score` `RiskGauge`, staggered `FactorBar` items with Simple/Detailed views, vertical 5-level `TriageLadder` with a `\"You are here\"` marker, action plan, and doctor questions.\n   - Added `WhatIfPanel` with live sliders and toggles for modifiable factors (`exerciseDays`, `sleepHours`, `smoking`, `alcohol`, `heatExposure`, `stressLevel`), calling `assessRisk()` on-device to show Before \342\206\222 After band and score changes with an `\"Illustration only, not medical advice.\"` notice.\n\n5. **Care Navigator, Privacy, Evidence & Quick Hide**\n   - Updated `CareNavigatorPage` with matte cards, an interactive 4-step pathway timeline, discreet teleconsultation booking, and `\"Sample data\"` badges on fictional clinics.\n   - Updated `PrivacyDashboardPage` with a plain-language inventory table, a visible **\"What left your device\"** panel, live consent toggles, JSON export, and full local wipe.\n   - Updated `EvidencePage` charts to use theme CSS variables and direct bar labels, paired with a **\"Method and limits\"** disclosure noting simulated rules do not prove real-world clinical accuracy.\n   - Updated `Navbar` and `QuickHideButton` so the Quick Hide label remains visible on mobile screens and double-tapping/double-clicking the HAYAT logo also activates Quick Hide alongside `Esc`.\n\n6. **Code Splitting & Verification**\n   - Added route-level `React.lazy` + `Suspense` splitting in `App.tsx` (separating `HeroDottedWave`, `EvidencePage`, and page routes into distinct chunks).\n   - Verified `compile_applet` (`vite build`), `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`), engine/conditional/i18n checks via `tsx`, and restarted the dev server cleanly on port 3000."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\376\002\n\373\002\001i\024}\023\241$\037\024\257\236\362\032\240\251z\334\005\000\203\225=W\370\250\a\355\234\037\321X!\035\257@ \t\216\331?\002\316E=\033z\305\277S\371\031Pt_\240\nf\216\024%[P\036\306\2202\177\332\v\032S\356o\rR\345Q\005\277\225\322\332\353?\350r\030\003\016_\037\005\215\003\315\033\344I\367_|\222\324\305\0063\372\024\370\224J*4O\204\312\306\035\234\027\202\024Ol\331\342\255I\023)\252JUg\353|\267>\250\203\033\017\224\372\303\364h\020\311d4%`{\271\243\356@P\016\206\342\341pt\377\320\355C\033\377\215\362\206M\372\"\004\261\006\275;\021>\266B \273\a\372\240=\301Sa\300\234\376\225\327\306\270P6Ml9o|\355\333\252Z@\302\006\377\0361z#L\213U\357\222\376m\231\357\334mq\266U\372CPw|\001 \023l\315\355\312D\362\320\366\210e\3323\300\304|\207\v\021W\231\212\271#\367(tNS\375\376\373\302\3155\267S\305P3\220\363>\365\234\230\377\334l\246x\226\223\206\351B\240\366\005]01\351\235\233hN@\357d*J\005\000\323\276\3156\350a\\_\376\004)\326\246\376e\020t\354o\346\002\203\222QF\232\253\'B*\376\332\341\367b\334\274\261/eh\267\376:l\306j}]\215y\223 \306\304U4\364\253\243lU\272"
