    thinking: "**Reviewing Core Requirements**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the clean install of `gsap` and `lenis`. My focus now shifts to a meticulous review of every user requirement. I\'m prioritizing 100% fidelity to the user\'s intent, starting with the motion principles: durations between 300-700ms, using the easing cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1), with no bounce.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Safety & Performance**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on safety and performance. I must ensure the app responds instantly to urgent events and user requests for quick hides, no matter the device or situation. I\'m also committing to optimizing for 60fps across the board with a single WebGL context. Lazy-loading is key, and I will be pausing animations when not visible, or on backgrounded tabs. Finally, I will cap the device pixel ratio at 1.5, and optimize for mobile devices by using lighter animation variants and disabling certain features.\n\n\n**Developing Motion Toolkit**\n\nI\'m deep in the weeds, architecting a reusable motion toolkit. I\'ve chosen `Framer Motion v12` with `AnimatePresence` and layout/presence animations, alongside `@react-three/fiber` for the `HeroDottedWave`. I\'m building out a series of components and hooks in `src/motion/`, including shared easing, durations, touch detection, and reduced motion preferences, culminating in a `<Reveal>` component, and a `<SplitText>` component. Accessibility is baked in from the ground up.\n\n\n**Constructing Motion Components**\n\nI\'ve made significant progress crafting individual motion components. I\'ve built `<CountUp>`, `<Magnetic>`, `<TiltCard>`, and `<PathDraw>` within the `src/motion/` directory, all carefully considering touch devices and reduced motion preferences. I\'ve also implemented a soft cursor glow follower and implemented calm full-page route transitions that gracefully respond to user preferences. These will also skip if a quick hide is active.\n\n\n**Implementing Background Wave**\n\nI\'m now implementing the subtle, site-wide background wave using `Canvas2D`. It\'s a low-contrast, animated dotted wave, with adjustments for tab visibility and reduced motion. I\'m carefully mapping route transitions to smooth shifts in hue and tint. The opacity is kept very low, ensuring text contrast.\nI am also constructing the details for the landing page hero and design. I\'m focusing on bringing the design to life with a WebGL dotted wave, and a headline revealed line by line. I will be incorporating parallax.\n\n\n**Designing Scroll-Driven Story**\n\nI\'m now focused on the scroll-driven story following the hero. I\'m building a 4-beat sequence within a pinned section using GSAP ScrollTrigger. The beats highlight the delay in fertility care, then a streamlined private approach. I am using a timeline to visually represent the timeline compressing. I am using explicit labels for \"illustrative/simulated\" time figures. I\'m ensuring graceful fallback on reduced motion, stacking the content instead of pinning. Arabic RTL support is being considered.\n\n\n**Refining Interaction Patterns**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on tactile feedback with a light and pleasing touch. I must also ensure primary CTAs use `<Magnetic>` on desktop.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'m focusing on the consent screen. I\'m building an animated SVG explainer with `<PathDraw>` for animated arrows representing data flow. I\'m using animated switches (`role=\"switch\"`, `aria-checked`) for the toggles, which include an animated confirmation tick. The \"I understand, continue\" button animates from disabled to enabled state. I\'m building a wizard screen that is a single question per screen, and ensures directional slide/fade transitions between questions. Selection animations will use green/teal borders, soft fills, and an animated checkmark SVG. I will also be including a wave-shaped progress line and a keyboard hint bar.\n\n\n**Refining User Interactions**\n\nI\'m now implementing logic to disable shortcuts while form inputs have focus to prevent accidental triggers. I\'m also focusing on the loading state transitions. The plain spinner is replaced with a Canvas/SVG sequence that converts scattered dots to a results gauge. This animation takes a maximum of 2.5 seconds, and has a skip button for early access to the result. I am also implementing an immediate urgent red-flag card for the results page.\n\n\n**Developing Results Screens**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the results page design. I\'m building a multi-stage process with key elements. The results gauge will morph from zero to the calculated value. Factor bars will animate in one by one. I am incorporating a triage ladder with a soft pulsing marker. I\'m also including an interactive \"What If\" panel with sliders, which will subtly tint the background based on the active risk band. I will present the patient with action plan cards and actionable buttons. I am also implementing an interactive, animated 4-step stepper component for the Care Navigator page.\n\n\n**Constructing Booking Flow**\n\nI\'m now building out the patient booking flow. I\'m developing a clear, step-by-step progress line: `Screened -> Booked -> Assessed -> Follow-up`. I\'m making sure it\'s RTL-aware. Clinic cards will use `<TiltCard>` and `<Reveal>`, and I\'ll label all clinics as `\"Sample data\"` and distances as `\"illustrative\"`. The teleconsultation is a mock booking only. I am keeping it safe, and not asking for personal fields.\n\nI\'ve also moved on to constructing the privacy dashboard. I\'m adding an animated data-flow SVG diagram to clarify anonymized research sharing. It starts by showing nothing leaving the device, but updates if anonymized sharing is enabled. Finally, I\'m implementing a calm \"dissolve\" animation to clean up data in the privacy dashboard; rows will break into particles and fade out upon deletion.\n\n\n**Implementing Export Confirmation**\n\nI\'m now focused on the sensitive export process. I must ensure the downloaded JSON clearly warns about sensitive health information. My plan includes a clear modal confirmation *before* the download, and prepending a `_notice` field to the exported JSON itself, avoiding changes to the service layer. I\'m exploring adding it directly within the `PrivacyDashboardPage`, which should keep the `api.ts` clean.\n\n\n**Refining Evidence Page**\n\nI\'m now implementing the evidence page. KPI cards will leverage `<CountUp>`, animated charts are being added with readable labels, axes and no text overlap. The fairness section will use group bars with a parity gap indicator and a checkmark. I\'m carefully maintaining the simulated data disclaimer. I am also doing a critical audit across all the code base, and am removing all \"proven\" statements.\n\n**How it Works Section**\n\nI\'m now building a pinned 4-step explainer leveraging GSAP ScrollTrigger for a step-by-step approach (`Private intake -> Rule-based engine -> Explainable guidance -> Targeted triage`). Each step will highlight as the user scrolls, paired with a small custom animated illustration, providing a clear visual representation of the process. I am also planning a mobile fallback for reduced motion.\n\n\n**Implementing Final Touches**\n\nI\'m now implementing the animated SVG explainer diagrams for each step. I\'m also creating a compact \"Safety and Limits\" section, along with an FAQ accordion with smooth height animations using `AnimatePresence` and `motion.div`.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'ve also moved on to implementing the quick hide feature, which involves an instant switch and a neutral wellness screen and return link. Finally, I\'m focusing on polishing the overall design. This includes implementing a consistent spacing scale, card radius, button styles with hover/press and focus-visible states. I am also implementing custom skeleton/shimmer loading fallbacks, friendly empty states, and a tidy 404 route for unknown paths, and adding page titles, meta descriptions, a custom favicon, and custom OG share for all pages.\n\n\n"
